## Summary

The bug was in `LocalConnection::poll` at `src/Client/LocalConnection.cpp`. When a query fails, the exception is stored in `state->exception`. On a *subsequent* `poll` call, the early exit at the top of the method immediately set `next_packet_type` to `Protocol::Server::Exception` and returned, delivering the exception packet to the client **before** any buffered log messages were flushed — so the trace/debug logs accumulated before the failure were discarded.

The fix adds a `needSendLogs` check to that early exception branch, mirroring the logic already present after the execution loop:

```cpp
if (state->exception)
{
    /// Flush any buffered log messages before delivering the exception,
    /// so that logs accumulated before the failure are not discarded.
    if (needSendLogs())
        return true;

    next_packet_type = Protocol::Server::Exception;
    return true;
}
```

`needSendLogs` drains the log queue into `Log` packets (returning `true` while there are pending logs, `false` once empty), so the exception is now deferred until all buffered logs have been sent. This ensures that with trace-level logging enabled, a failing query (e.g. `UNKNOWN_TABLE`) emits its Debug/Trace log lines to stderr in addition to the exception.

